// integration-tests/cft-reconfigure -- shared type. Deliberately minimal (a
// bare sequence number), unkeyed, single instance -- the point of this
// scenario is set_expression_parameters()'s runtime reconfiguration
// semantics, not the payload (same discipline every other scenario's own
// idl/ follows). Also reused, unmodified, as the "go-ahead" signal topic's
// type (see subscriber's GoTopic) -- same minimalism convention
// sample-rejected-lost's SyncTopic follows by reusing StatusEvent. Byte-
// identical copy required in every language's own idl/ dir, matching every
// other integration-tests scenario's convention. See
// docs/design/integration-test-tier.md.
@final
struct CftEvent {
    int32 seq;
};
